Z||000018||artherd||12-03-2001||09:20 PM||||Well, my (88 of course) Fourmula dosen't!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Droped it into second on the freeway when I had just put in the Red Line MTL tranny fluid (syncros work so well with it that it allowed the shift, with old crappy fluid the blocking rings won't let me do that)  at about 60mph...<P>Was good for what had to be about 7,000+rpm.<P>On a stock 2.8.  <P>Mobil 1 oil probally saved the motor.<P>PS: it sounded pretty cool  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (too bad out motors poop out at a weenie-arse 5200rpm or so. Absolutely NO power past there.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000019||Nashco||12-03-2001||10:08 PM||||Ha, yeah, I hate that.  After you get a bit past 5 grand, the thing keeps getting louder and louder like something's going to happen but doesn't do it.    It's like I keep waiting to burst into some sort of time-space continuum, but just keep getting louder and louder noise <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I keep the throttle mashed as long as I think I can, I hate low RPM chugging.  I love the 3700-5000 RPM range in second gear with our cars..feels the best to me, personally.<P>My 88 also doesn't have the RPM limiter, and it's a good thing, I hate RPM limits.  If I'm stupid enough to keep on it so long my motor explodes, so be it, but I hate limitations.  I used to run my VW flat four motor at 6000+ all day long without damage, then got an old Honda that would rev really high despite some major vibrations (1980 car), so I've been spoiled <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So, why do you want a rev limiter?  If you don't like the range the car is getting to, let off the throttle!!!! LOL<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000020||artherd||12-04-2001||12:47 AM||||Well... my Northstar car is definately going to have a limiter!<P>But then again, it's not going to have a *flywheel* (just a starter ring gear and a 7.25" clutch button pack) so it should get from idle to redline and back again about ten times in the time it takes "oh **** " to start forming on your lips  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I actually like limiters, they prevent you from grenading the engine if you blow a shift, and in racing (let alone normal driving) you never should hit them if you're driving for speed anyway.<P>PS: for stock Fieros, an MSD-6AL (HAVE to get the AL version) will do you great.  If you have a DIS 4-cyl engine however, your options are nearly nill as the MSD box won't work.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
